Good afternoon.  I am Jonathan Shapiera, a client of the NDIS.  I would lik=
e to discuss some statements related procedures of the NDIS.  Over the past=
 few weeks, we, the clientele, and Lived Experience of Forward Focused Grou=
p (FFG), who is my Service Provider, have been severely impacted and trauma=
tised by the actions of one Assistant Director in a branch of the NDIS.  A =
copy of the email below explains my communication to them on behalf of the =
Lived Experience.



The facts of the matter are thus:

=95        An organisation by the name of Nurse Assist 24/7=92s CEO verball=
y attacked my carer in a car park in Rockingham in my presence a few weeks =
ago.

=95        A VRO was issued against this CEO Amanda Damon, which stands tod=
ay.

=95        Three of four of my carers had previously worked for Nurse Assis=
t 24/7 and have serious issues with the attitude, behaviour and competence =
of this CEO and Company.  Hence the reason they left.

=95        Mr. Nathan Halls, an Assistant Director of NDIA began emailing F=
orward Focused Group clients with unfounded allegations of fraud and corrup=
tion and explaining they had to move house.

=95        I was contacted by NDIA=92s Nathan Halls and told that FFG were =
fraudulent and corrupt.

=95        I asked about facts and evidence and Mr. Halls stated he has bee=
n investigating for over 4 months.

=95        At this stage, no evidence has been produced, no factual matters=
 were produced, and everything from NDIA was run on the smell of an oily ra=
g.

=95        No facts or evidence of fraud or corruption against FFG & The Hi=
ve have been substantiated or have been produced.

=95        I am to understand that several of FFG & The Hive clients were t=
old that to proceed with the relocation, My Halls would increase their fund=
ing.

=95        My funding has been increased by $200,000 over two years just to=
 move house.  Please see the email below.

=95        Mr Halls further stated that I was to relocate to another servic=
e provider of his choice to accommodation of another company that I am unsu=
re of.

=95        Mr. Halls advised that I was to be contacted by Ms. Sukhi Tear, =
CEO of Diversatas, who would be my Service Provider.

=95        He further stated that I would receive an upgrade to my plan =93=
if I played=94 along with these proceedings.

=95        Mr. Halls told Assist Plan Managers that payments to FFG was no =
longer allowed.  Reimbursement of funds from invoices presented by FFG to t=
he Plan    Manager was stopped.

=95        FFG without funding, had all staff made redundant.  The Hive con=
tinued to trade.

=95        Ms. Barbara Lundgren, Nathan Halls manager, reinstated funding a=
nd the paying of invoices to FFG.

=95        FFG continues to trade and most of staff have returned.

=95        NDIA Assistant Director Nathan Halls continues to unsettle FFG a=
nd transfer clients from FFG control to another source via Diversatas.

=95        Diversatas do NOT disclose that they act on behalf of the Federa=
l Government

=95        4 clients were lost via this method this week.



The emotional statements are as follows:

=95        The Lived Experience are very pissed off that we, can be uproote=
d and distributed to places of uncertainty at a moment=92s notice without f=
actual evidence.

=95        The trauma that has been incurred by all parties directly and in=
directly is a matter of disturbance that needs addressing.

=95        The relationship =93as friends=94 between Mr. Halls and several =
of these other NDIS registered organisations runs deep.

=95        Many employees of these other organisations have compiled hatefu=
l and vindictive slants at FFG employees.

=95        The CEO of Forward Focused Group, Mrs Vida Reid, has received de=
ath threats from an anonymous party through social media.

=95        The staff of FFG are in the midst of creating a petition that re=
quests the NDIA to look at this matter and bring it to a stop.

=95        NDIA is currently refusing to interfere.

=95        As of 14th October the email below has not been responded to, he=
nce the reason for seeking media support.

=95        Mr Halls has on several occasions disclosed confidential informa=
tion and continues to do so without consequence.

=95        My son and I have suffered greatly over the years to the extent =
of being homeless for nearly 3 years living in our car.  In 2014 I wrote a =
document to the Federal Senate commenting on homelessness.  I was hoisted i=
nto the position of advocate and from there have worked towards helping oth=
ers where necessary.  Forward Focus became the family for us that we have n=
ot had.  The attempted dismantling of FFG by those who seem jealous of the =
position of its creator, is a shambles.  It is disrupting and tearing down =
the bonds that are created to form the NDIS.  The necessity of the NDIS sta=
nds firm for those who are and have a disability.  My son, at age 27 is goi=
ng blind and is still waiting for NDIS approval.  This approval was promise=
d by Nathan Halls in the consideration that I co-operate.  Words to that af=
fect were stated during conversation.  For the sake of my son it would have=
 been thought that I would shut up and not make mention of this matter.  Ni=
kolaus and I discussed this at length and decided that even in the event th=
at he does not get the attention he deserves due to his degrading eye condi=
tion, it is far better to speak for those who have little or no voice at al=
l, the Lived Experience.  This matter has come to the stage that it is impa=
cting staff, clients and other family members from an indirect purpose.  Th=
ose that are still involved with FFG remain loyal to the creators Simon & V=
ida Reid.  Mrs Reid has received award recently for Businesswomen of the Ye=
ar. Her accomplishments are to be acknowledged, not disputed and certainly =
not to be made a mockery of.



The article below is to be released 15th October and quite frankly I haven=
=92t seen more bullshit by NDIA than frogs on a lily pad.  They have contin=
ued to dismantle FFG at their own discretion but remain incognito when the =
media arrive.  No explanation has been offered.  The Lived Experience are s=
uffering consequentially because of the unprofessionalism of the WA branch =
of the NDIA.  We, as those with a disability will go all out to fight









+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++=
++++++++++++++++++++++++

Good day to you Miss Lundgren,



I am Jonathan Shapiera, and I am one of Forward Focused Group clients.  I a=
m extremely pleased to hear the news that FFG and The Hive are now able to =
operate again and trade.  As a representative and advocate of the FFG clien=
ts, I can say clearly that it has been a week of pure uncertainty.  It is n=
ot necessary for any disability client to state the trauma that they, as a =
person have gone through prior to these circumstances taking fold. Companie=
s like FFG & The Hive work towards alleviating such trauma that is, in many=
 cases, suffered daily.  This particular trauma that we have suffered in th=
e face of being relocated to houses and operations that we are unfamiliar w=
ith, is a disaster on its own. This is majorly due to your staff member Nat=
han Miles who seems to have taken it upon himself to run an operation that =
can only be described as an abuse of power.  I believe the necessity for in=
vestigations into that power that your staff has, needs clarifying.  This i=
s an Assistant Manager gone wrong.  Mr Miles divulged to me that investigat=
ions of fraud and misrepresentation of funds against FFG and The Hive was t=
he reason for my particular relocation.  As a Federal Officer, I question h=
is abilities to carry on.



After viewing the recent media coverage about the NDIS, I certainly concur =
with the necessity, as Dylan Alcot stated, that Lived Experience must play =
an important factor in ensuring that your operations are well and truly kep=
t above board and done legally.  I make mention of the fact that my own NDI=
S plan has increased by some $100,000 per year for the simplicity of moving=
 house.  Ms Lundgren, this is Government monies that your staff member has =
distributed me to move operations from my existing provider home to one sup=
plied by an appointed Mr Miles Co-ordinator, Miss Suhki Tear. How the hell =
do I spend $100,000 of Government money moving house?  Or is this considere=
d as SHUT UP MONEY?  In all consideration of this money, I do believe this =
should be distributed to ALL FFG clients for the trauma and inconsideration=
 your staff member has caused.



I am an educated person who has worked in corporate for many years before r=
etirement.  I ask for you to consider the clients during this disturbance t=
hat were not able to make a determination on their own faculties.  They wer=
e told that the operations of FFG and The Hive were wrong, false, and illeg=
al.  I do have this on good note and only if necessary, would invoke legal =
proceeding on behalf of Lived Experience.



I would like to also make mention of my son, Nikolaus.  We have been trying=
 for well over eighteen months to get a written letter to support my sons s=
ight problem.  We submitted a NDIS application a few months ago based upon =
Nikolaus severe depression and anxiety which has been rejected.  Last week =
we were finally able to receive a report by an optometrist who says that my=
 son is legally blind with severely reduced sight at present.  Your Mr Mile=
s gave consideration to look at this report, which was forwarded to him via=
 Ms. Suhki Tear.  I was of the opinion, and I apologise that I cannot state=
 clearly due to my ever-present brain fog, that my son=92s application was =
to be approved.  Given the fact that he and his friend have been given an e=
xit notice from a Yaran Properties Supported Independent Living unit in Roc=
kingham, he has less than 2 weeks to find somewhere else to live.  As my so=
n and I spent in the vicinity of nearly 3 years homeless living in my car, =
I would sincerely hope that this episode is not repeated for a nearly blind=
 young man.



Before going to the media to report the inconsistencies with your organisat=
ion, I would like to hear your response.  I would like to ask that you do n=
ot furnish me with bullshit articles from the NDIS.  I am not in the mood t=
o go chasing through articles to examine who said what.  Kindly pertain you=
r response to a person who has suffered severely over the years to be consi=
dered an honest NDIS client looking for a favourable outcome that satisfies=
 all concerned.





Regards

Jonathan Shapiera

0422 877 302




